# Copy to ops/secrets.env (gitignored) and fill in. Every runtime secret lives
# here; src/watch.sh, src/serve.sh and src/daily.sh source it.
#
# ops/ntfy.env is the older name for the same file and is still read, so an
# existing install needs no migration.

# service -> phone. SUBSCRIBE to this one in the ntfy app.
MAGOUN_NTFY_TOPIC=magoun-<random>
# phone -> service: button taps and the board's `arm` handoff. Do NOT subscribe;
# subscribing echoes your own commands back as notifications.
MAGOUN_NTFY_CMD=magoun-cmd-<random>

# From https://api-v3.mbta.com. Requested, not self-served -- MBTA approves them,
# so treat a key as scarce rather than assuming one per device.
#
# Without it everything shares the anonymous 20 requests/minute, counted PER
# CLIENT IP. Where that budget actually goes, measured:
#
#   an open board   ~12.5/min, continuously   <- the heavy user
#   watch.py          6/min, but only while a plan is armed
#   server.py         ~0; nothing asks it for v3 data
#   record_rt.py      none at all; it reads cdn.mbta.com
#
# So if you have ONE key, the board is where it buys the most, and the backend
# can sit on the anonymous allowance because it is idle most of the time. The
# same key in both places is fine -- the limit is per key, usage is nowhere near
# it, and rotating just means changing it in two places.
#
# The BOARD cannot read this file. Set its key per device in the browser:
#   localStorage.setItem("magoun.mbtakey", "<key>")
# or paste it into the box the board shows when it is being rate-limited. Never
# publish it into model.json -- that file is served from a public origin, so a
# key in it is a key given away.
MBTA_API_KEY=
